province = 37
blurb = "The text explains that Kudzu is a vine plant that grows naturally in the mountains and fields. The roots are described as being as large as an arm, and white in color. These roots were dug up from winter until the time of spring budding, crushed on top of a stone board, washed in a barrel of water, and strained to remove the dregs. The result was dried and made into kudzu starch."
